## LogicalBounds substrate trait (round 202605041128 follow-up)

Today `<UFixed<I, F, S> as Bounded>::MIN/MAX` projects through the
inner Bits container bounds, so `<U16Warm as Bounded>::MAX` returns
`u32::MAX` (the Warm 16-bit container). A separate `LogicalBounds`
substrate trait returning the logical-width bounds (`2^(I+F) - 1`
for unsigned UFixed, `-2^(I+F) .. 2^(I+F) - 1` for signed IFixed)
would expose the type-level bounds without requiring container
unwrap. Surfaced by Round 7 (#325) reviewer NIT during the Bounded
blanket landing; not blocking; ships when a consumer needs it. Open
design questions: whether to land as a separate trait or extend
`BitPresentation` (which already carries `LOGICAL_WIDTH`); whether
saturating, wrapping, and strict bound semantics belong on the same
trait or split.

## NBits<N>: niche-filled Bits variant

Maybe of NBits niche-optimises to size_of of Bits, giving "optional
N-bit value without discriminant overhead." Use cases include
optional bitfield slots, hash slots, packed enum fields. Tracked as
task #323; gated behind viola TS ecosystem verified (#197) plus
substrate-readiness gate (#231) so it stays in the future-tasks pool
until the gate clears. Open design questions for the future round:
where the niche lives (all-zeros default; configurable via marker?),
interaction with multi-container backing on Bits N greater than 128,
and the BitsContainerFor projection shape.

