  with double-width intermediate, saturating variants on Precise).
  Tracked under #320 / #321 (bench-driven SIMD platform expansion
  + asm microkernels for hot ops). Bits at those widths is available
  standalone with the BitPrim impl shipping in #316 (count_ones,
  trailing/leading_zeros, bitwise ops, etc.); UFixed / IFixed
  add/sub/mul/div at 129..=65535 await the arith bridge.
- **Cross-Bits Widen / Narrow for wide widths.** Cross-strategy and
  cross-container widening / narrowing through WideBits /
  AlignedWideBits16 shapes. Tracked alongside #320.
- **Hot AVX-2 / AVX-512 alignment tiers.** Tracked under #320 with
  bench-driven evidence per audit H1. Current Hot is align(16)
  baseline only via AlignedWideBits16. If bench evidence justifies
  the storage overhead, opt-in `HotAvx2` / `HotAvx512` consumer-visible
  strategy variants ship as separate markers (toolbox-not-policer
  compliant).
- **HotTruncate strategy variant.** Possible future Hot variant that
  truncates wide widths to 128 for compute (lossy but native-fast).
  Deferred for research under #322. Not in current strategy lattice.
- **Sign axis on bit-level traits.** Round B introduced the Sign
  axis on Bits only. Mask\<W\> / BitLogic / BitAccess / BitSequence
